# the sticks for m48_joyhold.keys (the format is m48_joy.joy's), for a
# play on the port's own clock: every move and press is held for 0.3 to
# 1 s, many reads of the timer's routine (one every 0.0549 s).  Both
# sticks are there from the program's start.  A line that puts a stick
# back to rest is written exactly as the first two here: options_test.sh
# dumps half a second after those only (never in the middle of a hold)
0 0,570,570,0
0 1,600,500,0
# the first stick: left 0.3 s
26.000 0,100,570,0
26.300 0,570,570,0
# right, left, right, left, 0.5 s each (9.1 of the reads' periods), each
# begun a quarter of such a period later within it than the one before
27.000 0,1100,570,0
27.500 0,570,570,0
28.222 0,100,570,0
28.722 0,570,570,0
29.443 0,1100,570,0
29.943 0,570,570,0
30.665 0,100,570,0
31.165 0,570,570,0
# up 1 s, down 1 s
32.000 0,570,100,0
33.000 0,570,570,0
33.800 0,570,1100,0
34.800 0,570,570,0
# its button 1 s, then left with the button 0.5 s
35.600 0,570,570,1
36.600 0,570,570,0
37.400 0,100,570,1
37.900 0,570,570,0
# the second stick: left 0.5 s, down 1 s, its button 1 s
38.800 1,100,500,0
39.300 1,600,500,0
40.000 1,600,1000,0
41.000 1,600,500,0
41.800 1,600,500,1
42.800 1,600,500,0
